course: dictionary
lesson: 8728
title: September, the ninth month
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: September is one of the twelve months of the year. It is the ninth month, so it comes after August and before October. Months are names of times, so start them with a capital letter, as in «in September», «early September» and «last September».
explain: September has 30 days. In a maths problem, 30 is the number of days in the month, so if you do something each day, multiply the amount by 30 to get the total for September. Count the months on your fingers when a calendar question feels tricky.
explain: The seasons change at different times around the world. «Back to school» in September means autumn is starting in the UK, USA, Canada and Ireland. In Australia and New Zealand, the same month is the start of spring.
fact: September is the ninth month of the year.
fact: September has 30 days.
fact: In the northern half of the world (UK, USA, Canada, Ireland), September is the start of autumn and of the school year.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, September is the start of spring.
fact: «Zhōngqiū jié» is the Mid-Autumn or Moon Festival, in September or October at the full moon, when families share a mooncake cut into small pieces.
exercise: Which month comes straight after August? | *September | October | November | June
exercise: The old rhyme says, «Thirty days hath September.» How many days does September have? | *30 | 29 | 28 | 31
exercise: In Australia and New Zealand, which season starts in September? | Winter | Autumn | *Spring | Summer
test: Which is the ninth month of the year? | October | December | August | *September
test: At the Mid-Autumn Festival, which food do families cut into small pieces? | *A rich mooncake | Turkey dinner | Pancakes | Birthday cake
exam: Lucy starts school in «early September» in London. Which season is it there? | Winter | *Autumn | Summer | Spring
